; fas9_surfaces_iso.scr - facit script of step 9.16, third round (F9.18, Opus): what AutoCAD's isolines of lofts and of NURBS
;   surfaces do where the first two rounds have no file. Run it with  python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_surfaces_iso.scr
; One drawing, saved once (surfaces_iso):
;   A  a loft of three equal splines moved along one line, unevenly (z 0, 10, 40): straight in v; where AutoCAD puts the sections
;   B  a loft of three equal splines moved off a line (z 0, 20, 40, y 0, 10, 0): curved in v
;   C  B copied and converted to NURBS (CONVTONURBS): the curved NURBS AutoCAD draws from the body as saved
;   D  a loft of four equal splines moved along one line, unevenly (z 0, 5, 25, 30)
;   E  a loft of two different splines (ruled)
;   F  a spline revolved 120 degrees about a line beside it
